%N A399808 Number of unlabeled Hausdorff set systems on an n-set with neither the empty set nor the full set.
%C A399808 A set system F on X is Hausdorff if for every two distinct elements x,y in X there exist A,B in F such that x is in A, y is in B, and A intersect B is empty.
%C A399808 Two set systems are considered equivalent if one is obtained from the other by a permutation of the underlying n-set.
%F A399808 a(n) = Sum_lambda Fix(lambda)/z_lambda, where the sum is over all partitions lambda of n, z_lambda = Product_{i=1..n} i^m_i m_i! for lambda = 1^m_1 2^m_2 ... n^m_n, and Fix(lambda) is the number of Hausdorff set systems on [n], containing neither the empty set nor [n], that are fixed by a permutation of cycle type lambda.
%e A399808 For n=3, write 1,2,3 for the singletons and 12,13,23 for the 2-subsets. Representatives of the 6 equivalence classes are {1,2,3}, {1,2,3,12}, {2,3,12,13}, {2,3,12,13,23}, {1,2,3,13,23}, and {1,2,3,12,13,23}. Hence a(3)=6.
%Y A399808 Cf. A398881.
